    "Courses at Faculty of Multimedia Communications | UTB\nCourses at Faculty of Multimedia Communications | UTB\nCourses\nUpcoming\nImportant dates\n03\nNov\nevent\nBusiness Day 2026\n06\nNov\ntbu\nOpen Day at TBU\n06\nNov\ntbu\nOpen Day at TBU\nCalendar\nFacebook\nInstagram\nTwitter\nYoutube\nCourses at Faculty of Multimedia Communications\nLevel of offered courses\nInternational students are allowed to choose freely which courses to take – possible recommendations/restrictions noted in column Note(s). Bachelor students are allowed to take master’s courses and the other way around, so the column Degree programme states the level of the course and its difficulty. Master’s courses should be more complicated, and the requirements might be higher.\nSemester of study\nEach course will be taught in a defined semester. It could be either in the\nWinter\nor\nSummer\nsemester. It cannot be changed. Nevertheless, some courses are offered in\nBoth\nsemesters.\nCredit requirements\nThe\nrequired minimum\nnumber of selected credits is\n15 ECTS\nper academic semester. The maximum number is not defined, but we recommend 30 ECTS credits as the maximum.\nMedium of instruction\nThe medium of instruction for courses offered below is\nEnglish\n, unless otherwise stated.\nList of courses for international exchange students\nThe academic year 2026/2027 (Last update on 01/04/2026)\nCourse code (abbreviation)\nCourse name\nLecturer\nDegree programme\nECTS credits\nSemester\nNote(s)\nAnimation Studio (KAAT)\nXAN\nAnimation\nprof. ak.mal. Ondrej Slivka,ArtD.\nBachelor\n15\nBoth\nPortfolio required\nXDAD\nDrawing and Design for Animators\nMgA. Martin Kukal\nBachelor\n5\nBoth\nPortfolio required\nGlass Design Studio (KADS)\nXASK1\nGlass Design Studio 1\nprof. MgA. Petr Stanický, M.F.A.\nBachelor\n10\nWinter\nPortfolio required\nXASK2\nGlass Design Studio 2\nprof. MgA. Petr Stanický, M.F.A.\nBachelor\n10\nSummer\nPortfolio required\nShoe Design Studio (KAOB)\nXSM1\nPractical Shoe Making 1\nM